```java
class HeapAndStackMemory {
    record User(String name) {}

    static User createUser(String name) {
        User localReference = new User(name);
        return localReference;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        User returnedReference = createUser("Mina");
        System.out.println(returnedReference.name());
    }
}
```

After `createUser` returns, its frame is gone. The `User` is still reachable from `returnedReference` in the caller.

